My $0.02,

I would wait and see how the hammer architecture does.  It's AMD's first
try at 64 bit, and the first generation Itanics were not that impressive
from Intel. (It seems the next generation is more promising..hmmm wonder
if all that R&D they purchased from DEC/Compaq is paying off?)

As for 21264's not being affordable, I would take a close look at the
UP1500 (I hope I got that right)  For about 3k you can get something
that will smoke any Intel / AMD system out there (if what I have read
and have been told is true.)

What will you be mainly using the system for?  I think with a little
more active development Xfree will see a dramatic performance increase
on alpha (Mike is extremely overworked in this regard).  Faster and
faster PCI cards are being released, as well as AGP cards (see UP1500
above).

I have an LX164 with a 533 processor, so I feel your pain.  Intel and
AMD have beaten away at the older alpha's edge with pure clock speed.
What do you need the system to do?  This is something I'm also very
interested in as I've fallen in love with the alpha.

Ted

