It will be out when it is out.  Not being out does not mean it 
wont be.  And if you check Debian's stable release schedule 
record, I believe you'll find Red Hat releases official stable 
Alpha releases several times between Debian stable releases.  

That is more likely to continue than to change.  I laugh when I 
hear people say they're going to switch to Debian unstable 
because Red Hat Linux *stable* 7.2 isn't out yet for Alpha.  

It's like someone saying they're going to use Red Hat Rawhide 
because Debian stable isn't out yet.  Makes no sense.

<shrug>

I wanted to say "Show me the Potato, and I'll show the beef." but
it would have had to be "Woody" instead of "Potato", and that
wouldn't make much sense, so the bad play on words lost its
merits somewhere.  Oddly I felt the need to toss it out there
just for fun anyway.  ;o)


-- 
