I saw this same error message with GAIM. I debugged it and figured
out that it had to do with a call to get information about the
X screen saver (something GAIM was doing with determining whether
the app was idle or not). I got rid of the problem with GAIM by
recompiling with a switch to tell it not to bother with the screen saver.
Or there's also a property setting about how it checks the idle status
that fixes the crash.

I also reported it to the gaim folks. I don't know if they've done
anything about it.

