Hi:

    I stumbled upon the 7.2 Beta2 ISOs on the Dec ftp site. These were dated 
02-Feb-2002. I installed on a Maita (PWS 500au) and am very impressed...
Compared to RedHat releases of the past, it looks like they have been going
thru 7.2 and stomping all the bugs. The only thing that did not work was 
Netscape, which made me try Galeon. I like Galeon so I don't care if Netscape
is broken.

    I reboot it regularly to make sure the ext3 filesystem is working and I 
*really* like being able to just run authconf and have LDAP work out of the
box on the first try with my iPlanet directory server. 

    Again I am pretty happy with it, and I think that the release version will
be worth waiting for. There may not be another for a while so I don't mind if
they take the time to get it right.

Cheers,

</Duane>




