>
>I downloaded the latest XFree4.2 rawhide source rpm and tried to get it
>to build and it died (specfile suggested it might on alpha)
>
>Which is the most current one that builds on alpha?

It builds on alpha with gcc 2.96 just fine.  XFree86 contains 
some bugs on 64bit architectures however when compiled with
gcc 3.1.  Bad assumptions in the code.

Basically, XFree86 assumes that if _LP64 is defined, that the 
architecture is a sparcv9.  Very dumb.  Not hard to fix though, I 
just haven't bothered doing so yet.


