Speaking from a personal perspective - I don't care for your
attitude either.  I'm free to speak my opinion, it's a free
world.  Deal with it.

I don't find my statements to be "hacking other distros".  Read 
what I said again, and point out the error in my statement.  
There isn't any.


>	(a disappointed Redhat/Alpha **paying** customer).

If you're disappointed in a product, the solution is quite simple
really - don't purchase that product.  I certainly wouldn't.  I
feel quite confident however that for every one of our
disappointed customers, there are a large number of very happy
customers.  Ultimately, use what works for you.


>P.S. I like challenges, so off goes Redhat 7.0 cum 7.1, and on goes
