>
>I hardly think that taking your aggressions out on Mike (or any other 
>RedHat person on this this) is going to accomplish anything. If you just 
>want to complain and write with the caps lock on all day then kindly go 
>elsewhere. All of the RedHat people that I know about on this list do 
>their best to make sure things work properly, sure things go wrong and 
>people get frustrated but it's no good acting like that.
>
>Perhaps you (and others so obsessed with 7.2's release date) would be more 
>content if instead of calling it RedHat 7.2, they were to call it RedHat 
>7.4. That way it wouldn't be late (whatever that means) and you'd be ahead 
>of the x86 folks.....anyone??
>
>--rdp
>
>P.S. FWIW, you state above you have a PC164, last I knew RedHat was 
>supporing only EV6(+) systems in the 7.x series. 

Depends on the definition of "support" that you use.  The 
software should run on any EV5 or higher system really.  Wether 
or not it will install and work with a given system depends on 
the system.  That's no different than our x86 product though.  
Our packages will _run_ on an i386, however our minimum system 
requirements are Pentium class machine or higher.  We do not test 
anything out on i486 or lower machines, and not on older Pentium 
level systems either.

For Alpha, I'm not sure what types of machines are tested, but it
makes sense that the distro should run ok on Alpha systems which
we intend to support.  I'm sure either our website or the
HP/Compaq website will list those official systems.  Likewise to
x86 however, it will run on many systems aside from the
officially supported ones.


-- 
