With regards to your message at 09:23 PM 6/2/02, cprice@its.to. Where you 
stated:
>         I am not obsessed with Redhat 7.2 release date. I really wish the
>fscking wankers on this list would put discussion threads in context. My
>email above was in response to a Redhat person making disparaging
>remarks about another distro (Debian I beleive, but it does not matter).
>What I am saying is that *PEOPLE IN GLASS HOUSES SHOULD NOT THROW
>STONES*, as Redhat on Alpha has never been what I would call stable.


Let's not get too carried away here, OK?

I admit I was being a "pot stirrer" as mentioned, but none of us  should 
let any of this degenerate into a name calling or  cursing session..

I admit that it was my intention to put a bit of a hotfoot on some of the 
Red Hat guys, but that was meant to extract some info on why the release 
was being delayed.

Ultimately, as Mike explained, and as should be pretty obvious, any non-X86 
distro is not likely to be profitable, and in the case Compaq is paying for 
it. As such the pay the piper and they call the tune. In this case the tune 
is ES4x, mainly. As few of us have those beasts, it is likely not too 
important for most of us on this list.

However, once they have finished doing what the sole paying customer in 
this requires, I still think the rest of us will benefit to some large degree..

The fact that they are not releasing something to you with the speed you 
hope for, whether justified or otherwise, however does not give you the 
right, in a public forum, to call them names or swear.

Both Red Hat and Debian are doing a new AXP distribution model. As such we 
should appreciate that. They are all we have. The fact that neither is 
perfect is not surprising, and to expect much more is not reasonable.


My $.02 worth.


With our best regards,

