doesnt every company is some form or fashion stop supporting older hardware?
HPAQ stopped supporting older EV4 based systems, older HSZ's, etc with the
current releases of DUNIX (i still cant bring myself to say hp Tru64 UNIX).
Oracle doesnt bothering compiling for EV4 or EV5 based systems anymore...
it seems most companies compile for EV56 and above only and if you just
happen to have an old system, you're stuck with running the code with
instruction emulation -- PAINFULLY SLOW.

it's too expensive and time consuming to qualify every peice of older
hardware for a new version of software.  especially seeing the older
hardware in question is around 5-6 years old already.

the good thing about OpenSource is that you can compile your own code if you
want to stay current.

