On Mon, 3 Jun 2002, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:

>make: Leaving directory `/usr/src/rpm/BUILD/XFree86-4.2.0/xc'
>error: Bad exit status from /var/tmp/rpm-tmp.49956 (%build)
>
>
>RPM build errors:
>    Bad exit status from /var/tmp/rpm-tmp.49956 (%build)
>
>This is the diff output from the original specfile and the
> one that I modified:
>
>romulus:/usr/src/rpm/SPECS# diff XFree86.spec XFree86.spec.custom 
>3c3
>< ExcludeArch: alpha ia64
>---
>> #ExcludeArch: alpha ia64

That's ok, as the ExcludeArch is only there right now because X 
wont compile on 64bit arch's with gcc 3.1 currently due to a 
simple issue I've not resolved yet.  Building with gcc 2.96 
should be fine however, so commenting out the above is ok.

>1006c1006
>< #define BuildXF86DRI                YES
>---
>> %define BuildXF86DRI                YES

That is invalid.  Those defines are not RPM macros being defined, 
they are Imake macros which get put in the file host.def via a 
here document to configure the X build process.  Imake uses the C 
preprocessor, so they are ultimately C preprocessor defines, and 
should appear as:

#define foo bar

And to comment one out, you do so as in C:

/* #define foo bar */

>1008c1008
>< #define BuildXF86DRI                NO
>---
>> %define BuildXF86DRI                NO

Again, invalid.

>1052,1053c1052,1053
>< #define XF86CardDrivers mga nv tga s3virge sis rendition \
><                       neomagic i740 tdfx cirrus tseng trident chips
>apm \
>---
>> %define XF86CardDrivers mga rendition \
>>                       i740 tseng trident chips apm \

I don't see anything wrong there.  Replace the % with # on the
defines, and try to rebuild again.  What compiler are you using?


-- 
