On Tue, 4 Jun 2002, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:

>Date: Tue, 4 Jun 2002 21:33:23 -0500
>From: "Ted Goodridge, Jr" <tedgoodridgejr@acm.org>
>To: axp-list@redhat.com
>Content-Type: text/plain;
>	charset="us-ascii"
>List-Id: Linux and Red Hat on Alpha processors <axp-list.redhat.com>
>Subject: RE: XFree86-4.2.0-50.10.src.rpm errors doing build
>
>Mike, 
>	how do I get it NOT to build tdfx stuff, cause the build keeps
>dying at tdfx_context.h.

It is entirely possible that the tdfx code there uses code which
is/isn't ISO C, that the older gcc 2.95 you're using wont
compile.  It could be some other issue as well.

Post the full error you're seeing.  Often a failed X build the 
problem is not in the last 10 lines of the build, but might be a 
problem that happened 15 minutes prior to that, which didn't kill 
the build right away.  You need to go through the whole log file 
looking for errors/warnings.

tdfx_context.c contains code which is not compliant to ISO C99 I 
know for sure as it complains fiercely when it compiles it (but 
it works anyway).

You might want to check debian's patches to see if they patch 
this file for the older gcc.


