So, I've installed RH 7.0 on one AS 1200, and per Jay's suggestion I tried
7.1 both with the same Powerstorm card and two other cards -- but I
couldn't get it to work. Before we get to that question, whenever I
installed 7.1 OR 7.0, I get this funny message. With 7.0, I ignored and
the install worked but at boot the abot points at the wrong drive. It will
boot when I point it at the right one. But in 7.1, doesn't matter what I
do; after install, reboot simply cannot find a valid boot image on any
drive.
Here's the error I see just prior to installation formatting. Any ideas?

Fdisk error

And error occurred reading the partition table for the block device sdb.
The error was:
"Partition(s) do not end on cylinder boundary."

This error occurs because the drive geometry detected by the kernel used
by the installer is different than the drive geometry used when the drive
was partitioned. This can be corrected by specifying the drive geometry on
the kernel command line when booting the installer.
As I said, I got the other machine to run, but it ALSO had this error, and
although the system works, I have that weird boot problem AND it only
seems to address drives sda and sdb…. Even though I have seven drives in
the RAID array. Any thoughts?
Thanks in advance, Ralph





