Hi all,

I just came along a shiny AlphaStation 500/333 (much better than my
old Multia and AlphaServer 1000/200).

Unfortunately, I'm unable to run a 2.4 kernel on that system. 2.2
works fine, but 2.4 crashes while probing the SCSI bus (I've tried
with both the internal QLogic and a Symbios 53c875 based card, with
kernel 2.4.17, 2.4.18 and 2.4.19-pre10, with both Generic and Alcor
options).

Here's the message I'm getting with the 875 card :

SCSI subsystem driver Revision: 1.00
sym.0.12.0: setting PCI_COMMAND_INVALIDATE.
sym0: <875> rev 0x4 on pci bus 0 device 12 function 0 irq 20
sym0: No NVRAM, ID 7, Fast-20, SE, parity checking
CACHE TEST FAILED: DMA error (dstat=0xa0).sym0: CACHE INCORRECTLY CONFIGURED.
sym0: giving up ...

A kernel compiled with qlogic crashes with a machine-check exeption
(660, IIRC).

I also get this message while initializing the PCI chipset (don't know
if that's normal or not) :

pci: passed tb register update test
pci: failed sg loopback i/o read test (0x5cee00 != 0xdeadbeef)
pci: disabling sg translation window

If that's of any interrest, I'm booting off SRM V6.9-5 (serial
console).

Does anybody have a clue or, even better, a known working .config for
that system ?

Thanks a lot,

        M.
-- 
Places change, faces change. Life is so very strange.




