On Sun, Jun 09, 2002 at 03:30:02PM +0100, Damien Dye wrote:
> hi all
> 
> what's the equivalent package to bin86 for alpha

none.

> with bin86 being the x86 assembler I recon there is a package out there but

as86 (of the bin86 package) is a so called 'real-mode' assembler for the 
80x86 16-bit mode that those processors are in when they leave the reset state. 
as86 is (or at least was) used to generate early boot code to prepare 
transition to the so called 'protected' mode.

AFAIK Alpha processors don't have the equivalent of a stupid real mode with 
different memory management, different register size and layout etc.
So: no seperate assembler :)

> what's it called.
> 
> Thanks all

Bye,
Thorsten

