On Sun, Jun 09, 2002 at 02:53:09PM +0200, Marc Zyngier wrote:
> 
> I finally succeded into booting 2.4.19-pre10 by simply disabling the
> DAC window, even if memory fits into the window. This is ugly, but it
> allows me to boot the system (see included patch). I'd really like
> someone with proper knowledge to give it a look.

It is a known problem, though patches have yet to appear.

The Alpha PCI rewrite in 2.4.13, IIRC, was indeed the culprit, adding
the DAC code and reworking the use assignment of the PCI DMA windows.

Unfortunately, the CIA-1 core logic in AS500/333 as well as EB164 and
XLT (Hi, Doc! :-) is flawed, and the current assignment of use to
windows exposes this flaw.

I will post patches against 2.4.19-preX when I get in to work Monday.

Sorry, at the moment I have no answers for the serial-related problems.

 --Jay++

