Hi!

"\"Thursday\" AKA dr. john" wrote:
> 
> To the list:
> 
> Has this ever happened to you?
> 
> This is a PWS 500 a/u running RH 7.1  I lost the magenta (red) signal
> from my Oxygen VX1 video card a couple weeks ago ... [...]
> 
> Has anything like this happened to anyone else on the list?

Two years ago, I had it the other way round: The "red" remained, 
other colours wer reduced or lost (happened on a x86 PC). 
I attributed it to monitor problems, and with another monitor 
it did not show again.

AFAIK, with a standard VGA sub-D 15 pin interface (and with BNC also), 
each colour is transferred via its own wire / plug pole. 
Have you considered the chance of either developing contact problems 
and a higher resistance? 
Is the cable is not fixed to the monitor, you might try changing that.

In any case, I would be surprised if that were a motherboard problem, 
because AIUI there is no motherboard part or contact which is specific 
to a single colour (others - please correct me if I am wrong here).

HTH, 
Joerg Bruehe

