On Sun, Jun 09, 2002 at 10:31:59AM -0600, Thursday AKA dr. john wrote:
>
> This is a PWS 500 a/u running RH 7.1  I lost the magenta (red) signal
> from my Oxygen VX1 video card a couple weeks ago ... thought it was a
> bad card, then swapped things around, ran the card in a PC and watched
> it slowly recover its red signal while running the intro to my kid's
> Heavy Gear 2 game. 

By "slowly recover", do you mean that even in the PC the color was
screwy initially, and then came back, like fading in?

Was this with the same monitor that the original problem appeared on?

> I put the card back in my PWS and the color was back ... for about a
> week.

Weird. What happens with a different card, but same monitor, in the PWS?

> Today i was idly watching the script while booting.  The one where the
> passed or failed is in color ... All of a sudden, in 1 or 2 seconds, the
> color faded out.  Back to Blue.

Have you tried twisting/turning/adjusting the bends in the VGA cable,
especially close to the head that attaches to the monitor? Reason I ask,
all my prior experiences with similar color problems could be traced to
a cable going bad.

> I wonder, is this a video card problem, or is something happening in the
> PCI bus?  This particular PWS has had other chipset-type problems.

IMHO, wouldn't be on the PCI bus, but could be a problem on the VGA card
itself.

