> On Mon, 10 Jun 2002, Jay Estabrook wrote:
>
> >> Today i was idly watching the script while booting.  The one where the
> >> passed or failed is in color ... All of a sudden, in 1 or 2 seconds, the
> >> color faded out.  Back to Blue.
> >
> ...
>
> I concur.  Sounds like the video adaptor is flaky, or possibly 
> the connection to the monitor or monitor cable.

One thing I didn't think of the first time: You might use a
magnifying glass to check the solder joints between the VGA
socket and the printed circuit board.  One fairly common
problem with many connectors is a cracked solder joint where
the connector pin meets the board trace or pad.  If this is
the problem, a steady hand with a fine-pointed soldering iron
(properly grounded, of course) may be the solution.  (Of
course, doing soldering youself will probably void any warranty.)

Good luck.

Robert Riches
