There is a list of old machines on which I tested, on the CDs, named
something like Alpha-HW-Notes.

As to the AS2100 5/250, it was one of the machines I tested on, and should
be fine, with a few caveats and things to avoid. If it has more than 1GB
of memory, you should add the "mem=1G" argument to the boot command line
for both the install and subsequent reboots. Second, it will probably be
much safer to use "text mode" install, as some of the servers are having
problems running on SABLEs.

Good luck.

