On Tue, Jun 11, 2002 at 10:39:41AM -0400, Jay Estabrook wrote:
....
> Other platforms that also seem to work well include the
> other EV6-based boxes (XP1000, UP2000, and UP1000/1100, though the latter
> two "Nautilus" machines don't seem to work with AGP versions of those cards,
> just PCI versions)

You should expect AGP versions of cards to work on "Nautilus" boxes when
used with kernels (they change over time and they are not absolutely
"quirk free" yet :-) which can be found at

   ftp://ftp.harddata.com/pub/kernel_Nautilus/

Although I have only one model of Nautilus (UP1500) to test I am pretty
confident that this is the case.  These kernels are actually "generic"
and will work over wider range of models although recent fixes from Jay
to CIA boxes are not yet included in this moment.

Depending on your video card you may want to consider using 4.2.0
version of XFree86 rpms for which can be found at Red Hat "rawhide".

