On Tue, 11 Jun 2002, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:

> 	7.2 comes with Xfree 4.1.  If I want to upgrade to 4.2 using
> source rpms, what are the necessary steps?  (I know how to do a build
> etc, but I want to make sure that when I actually do the upgrade, I
> follow the right course of action.)
>
> 	(I guess I was smoking crack with my earlier comment about X4.2
> and redhat 7.2...oops)

7.3 comes with Xfree86 4.2, but I fear I am opening another can of worms.

You can grab the Xfree86 4.2 src.rpms from either Rawhide or 7.3, and
install them on your system.

rpm -Uvh Xfree86-4.2.0-$somenum.src.rpm

Then cd /usr/src/redhat/SPEC and open the Xfree86.spec file in your
favorite text editor.

Read it, and change flags. comment in or out what seems prudent, and then
do an rpm -bb /usr/src/redhat/SPEC/Xfree86.spec

(builds the binary rpms from the spec file, rpm -ba builds binaries and
source rpms)

If the compiles work, go to /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha, and do an rpm -Fvh
* and see how that goes.

--
-- John E. Jasen (jjasen1@umbc.edu)
