> > other EV6-based boxes (XP1000, UP2000, and UP1000/1100, though the latter
> > two "Nautilus" machines don't seem to work with AGP versions of those
> > cards, just PCI versions)
> 
> You should expect AGP versions of cards to work on "Nautilus" boxes when
> used with kernels (they change over time and they are not absolutely
> "quirk free" yet :-) which can be found at
> 
>    ftp://ftp.harddata.com/pub/kernel_Nautilus/

My above quote was truncated a bit, but what might be a bit more
clear, is that I've had no luck in getting a Matrox G200 or G400 AGP
card to do 3D via the AGP GART support of the AMD core logic on an
UP1100.

Some PCI cards which use their own PCI GART support, do work fine on
those boxes; this includes ATI Rage128 and Radeon cards.

I think it's also possible to make an AGP card actually use the PCI
GART HW and code and do 3D, but I've never tried. because I can't get
the console's BIOS emulation to work with the AGP versions of the ATI
cards, which are the only ones I know with PCI GART support.

Michal, do you mean that your kernels *DO* support 3D via AGP GART,
and that the UP1500 *DOES* have BIOS emulation that'll work on the
ATI cards, or perhaps you've had better luck with AGP GART and the
Matrox cards?

