> 
> 7.3 comes with Xfree86 4.2, but I fear I am opening another can of
worms.
> 
> You can grab the Xfree86 4.2 src.rpms from either Rawhide or 7.3, and
> install them on your system.
> 
> rpm -Uvh Xfree86-4.2.0-$somenum.src.rpm
> 
> Then cd /usr/src/redhat/SPEC and open the Xfree86.spec file in your
> favorite text editor.
> 
> Read it, and change flags. comment in or out what seems prudent, and
then
> do an rpm -bb /usr/src/redhat/SPEC/Xfree86.spec
> 
> (builds the binary rpms from the spec file, rpm -ba builds binaries
and
> source rpms)
> 
> If the compiles work, go to /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha, and do an rpm
-Fvh
> * and see how that goes.
