I cannot find a file like the one it is complaining about.  My old
aboot.conf had no reference to initrd or console so I tried removing
that part of a line.  When I boot like that, it complains that the root
parameter is invalid and it cannot find /dev/sdb1.

My setup was as follows on the old RedHat 7.0 install and it worked
fine.
/dev/sda1 is /boot and /dev/sda2 is swap
/dev/sdb1 is the root
/dev/sdc1 is /home

Any suggestions?  I'm tempted to just do a re-install but I'd rather try
to fix this if I can.

