>Date: Tue, 11 Jun 2002 12:04:45 -0500
>From: "Ted Goodridge, Jr" <tedgoodridgejr@acm.org>
>To: axp-list@redhat.com
>Content-Type: text/plain;
>	charset="us-ascii"
>List-Id: Linux and Red Hat on Alpha processors <axp-list.redhat.com>
>Subject: Xfree 4.2
>
>Mike et all,
>
>	7.2 comes with Xfree 4.1.  If I want to upgrade to 4.2 using
>source rpms, what are the necessary steps?  (I know how to do a build
>etc, but I want to make sure that when I actually do the upgrade, I
>follow the right course of action.)

The Red Hat Linux 7.3 XFree86 4.2.0 src.rpm works compiled for 
Alpha.  You can simply take the src.rpm, and rebuild it, however 
you'll need to update it with other deps from 7.3 first.

One other noteable thing, is that you'll need to disable DRI 
because DRI in 4.2.0 requires a newer kernel (unless our Alpha 
kernel had it backported, which very well could be true - I'm not 
sure however).

If in doubt, try it.  If DRI works - great!  If not, bummer.  ;o)




-- 
