On Wed, Jun 12, 2002 at 11:57:20AM -0500, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> Would that have the updates (freetype) and would it have DRM support
> built in?

DRM is a question of a cooperation between your kernel and your X
driver.  I hope that Mike will not get an idea of wholesale disabling
it in binaries compiled for Alpha because this would kill that option
even if situations where this works.

So far I have on the same machine and with the same kernels this
in logs if I am using Radeon card:

(II) RADEON(0): X context handle = 0x00000001
(II) RADEON(0): [drm] installed DRM signal handler
(II) RADEON(0): [DRI] installation complete
(II) RADEON(0): [drm] Added 32 65536 byte vertex/indirect buffers
(II) RADEON(0): [drm] Mapped 32 vertex/indirect buffers
(II) RADEON(0): Direct rendering enabled

but when I replace it with MGA G450:

(EE) MGA(0): [drm] failed to remove DRM signal handler
(II) MGA(0): [drm] removed 1 reserved context for kernel
DRIUnlock called when not locked
(II) MGA(0): [drm] unmapping 8192 bytes of SAREA 0xfffffffc003a8000 at
0x20000024000
  ....................
(==) MGA(0): Direct rendering disabled


so your mileage may vary.  But even if DRM fails I do not see harm
otherwise.  Turning that support off would ensure that you will fail in
every case. :-)

   Michal




