DRI works on Alpha, so I wouldn't disable it.  The challenge of
having proper kernel installed with proper DRM modules however
will be left as an exercise to the reader.  ;o)  You'll all have 
to convince Arjan or Bryce to roll a DRM 4.2.0 kernel if the 
current one doesn't have it (I haven't checked).  ;o)


>so your mileage may vary.  But even if DRM fails I do not see harm
>otherwise.  Turning that support off would ensure that you will fail in
>every case. :-)

Please report DRI related bugs to dri-devel@dri.sf.net

;o)


