Mike A. Harris wrote:
 >
 > My guess would be VR goggles.
 >

Well sort of.  I think they were LCD shutter glasses.  The card would
display the image for the left eye on the screen while applying current
to the right eye's shutter (so it would be dark), then it would reverse,
showing a slightly shifted view of the scene for the right eye while
blanking the left.

Cool cheap technology.  Sega used it with their Master System (8-bit),
worked amazingly well, even if it limited frame rates to 15 fps on TV.
With today's monitors refresh rates things are much better.




