> Freeing unused kernel memory: 368k freed
> Kernel panic: No init found.  Try passing init- option to kernel.


It's highly likely that you don't have an adaptor driver loaded
You may need to 'force' the issue with something akin to

mkinitrd -f -v --preload sd_mod --preload aic7xxx --preload sym53c8xx 
--preload jbd --preload ext3 /boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.img 2.4.9-32

You need the correct adaptor driver loaded in with the ramdisk otherwise 
it won't be able to read the data of the disk because it won't know how 
to access it.

sd_mod needed for any scsi device
aic7xxx		adaptec scsi driver
sym53c8xx 
ncr/symbios scsi driver
jbd and ext3	part of the ext3 FS layer

To get around this in future, you should update the /etc/modules.conf 
and insert
alias scsi_hostadapter aic7xxx
(or whatever it's supposed to be)


Phil
=--=




