>you should be able to mount the isos using /dev/loop. I'd have to
look
>back at exactly how to do it as it's been awhile, but it is possible
to do
>it.

mkdir ./loopdir
mount -o loop XYZ.iso ./loopdir

One caveat: nfs installs know how to handle this, but I am afraid for
ftp/http isntalls, you have to copy the files from the CDs (or from
the loop-mounted directories) into one "regular" "RedHat" directory
tree.

Ingo




