Earl Truss wrote:
> Yes, it does but I think the problem occurs before the root disk is
> mounted.
> 

I have not installed RH for the Alpha, BUT on another dist I ran into 
some similar problems when using initrd for the first time.  The problem 
turned out to be on the startup command line.  Make sure you give the 
full path to the initrdXXXX.img file in this command relative to your 
root directory.  If you have it located in /boot then the command should 
be something like "initrd=/boot/initrdXXXX.img" if you are using the 
actual file.  Alternatively, you can create a symlink to it from the / 
(root) directory and reference this symlink on the command line.

I use MILO here and don't know anything about the SRM console, so this 
second "observation" may or may not apply.  The initrd.img file can get 
quite large depending on how much you have compiled into the kernel as 
modules.  On my 2.4.18 kernel, I had one that was about 4.8 Megs, I 
think.  Anyway, the default MILO ramdisk size was set to 4 Megs and it 
couldn't load the img file because it was too big.  I had to specify a 
larger ramdisksize on the command line.  Dunno if this affects you or not...

Cheers & Good Luck!
-Don Spoon-






