Hi,
I think for one of the places, you're already OK: this list ;-) Then, there 
are all kinds of HOWTOs around and man-pages and info-pages. Then there is 
Google and http://www.tldp.org/ and all the others.
 Honestly: I think it's kind of an art to find what you're looking for. But, 
most important of all, you have to know WHAT you are looking for. And this 
may take up most of the time you spend hunting down the problem!
 If you think now: "I want my system to boot", this is good, but too general. 
You have to know WHY you can't boot. And perhaps the real problem is not 
where you think, but elsewhere. So be sure to understand the things that lead 
up to your problem.
 Too general what I'm talking about? And yet, this was a bit of your question, 
no?
 I have to admit, I didn't find yet the holy grail of linux documentation. I 
tend to beleive that it doesn't exist. It's back to our ancestors: hunting 
time. This is why I love linux ;-)

Happy hackin'

Ineiti





