Let's go over the checklist again:

1) Did you boot into rescue mode with the CDROM?

2) Did the rescue mode mount your filesystems on disk?
	It will say something like "mounted / on /mnt/sysimage"
	It will say something like "mounted /usr on /mnt/sysimage/usr"

3) Did you type "cdroot /mnt/sysimage" at the shell prompt?

4) Can you list the SCSI driver modules in /lib/modules?
	type "ls -l /lib/modules/2.4.9-32/kernel/drivers/scsi"
	Is ncr53c8xx.o in that directory?

5) Does the mkinitrd command now succeed?

mkinitrd -f -v --preload sd_mod --preload aic7xxx --preload sym53c8xx
--preload jbd --preload ext3 /boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.img 2.4.9-32

6) If so, reboot off the hard disk.

Bob




