Actually since it seems to be wanting the use of the ncr driver you 
could try and modify the above mkinitrd line to

mkinitrd -f -v --preload sd_mod --preload aic7xxx --preload sym53c8xx 
--preload ncr53c8xx --preload jbd --preload ext3 
/boot/initrd-2.4.9-32.img 2.4.9-32


Part of the problem in trying to help you is that you've not really
told us what scsi card you have in box. The more info you can supply,
the better we can formulate a response.

I can't remember if lspci is available from the rescue option or not
but if you get past step 3 above then you should be able to run it
from the command prompt. That would give us a better idea of what needs 
tweeking. Oh, and can you show whats in /etc/modules.conf on your disk?

(assuming the extra --preload ncr53c8xx doesn't get you anywhere)

Phil
