On Wed, Jun 19, 2002 at 08:37:14AM -0700, Goran Marnfeldt wrote:
> Something in this behavior tells me that 2.5.21 is
> no meant for me :-)

2.5.x kernels do not compile on Alpha without bigger or smaller
"adjustments".  If you will dig a bit in archives of linux-kernel
list you can find patches, posted by Ivan Kokshayski, which allow
to compile and run on this architecture too.

Saying that I would stay away from 2.5.21 unless you plan to help to
debug it (and you are a bit late for that).  All kernels from 2.5 series
are, obviously, development kernels and may eat your file systems and do
other unspeakable things to your machine but 2.5.21 would need, ahem, an
extra care.  If you still want to do that then watching for a while
linux-kernel list before you embark on such adventure is highly
recommended.

  Michal




