<Grumble>
If I had a red cent for every variation of a tulip ethernet NIC that was 
ever made for the alpha, I'd have enough for a decent snack at subway.

In the beginning there was the 21140 and it was good, and it was stable
then they decided that a 21141 would be a good thing bit couldn't get it 
to work so they made the 21142 and it was woeful, but many people 
thought 'Hey! lets make clones!' and they did and each and every one of 
them was subtly different and some worked and some didn't, and this 
continued into the 21143 range.

Don't get me wrong, *IF* you have a genuine tulip, they are amazingly 
fast and stable but the number of varients and slight changes between 
revisions makes creating a generic tulip driver close to impossible.

Bottom line. There are too many 2114X varients to be supported. Try and 
get a hold of a network card fo which there are fewer viarents eg the 
3com Cyclone (3c905B) or the 59x that you mentioned would also work well.

Phil
