At least with those DEC tulip cards which I have seen in 2.4 series, as
opposed to 2.2 kernels where 'tulip' driver was the one to use, 'de4x5'
driver is working quite nicely and this includes autonegotiation.
Beyond versions included in very early 2.4 kernels I did not manage to
send a single ethernet packet using 'tulip' driver either on x86 or on
Alpha.  This is using tulips from DEC and not "clones".  In 2.5 kernels
'tulip' seems to start to work again.

OTOH current 'tulip' from 2.4 works, in my experience, with all these
PNICs and LiteOns which previously were a source of constant headaches.
YMMV.  It is very likely that what is on the other end of a wire (a
model of a hub or a switch and how it conducts negotiaitons) may affect
this behaviour.

