"lot of experience" Maybe I wrote it. I didn't mean I'm an expert.  I have
3 alphas (1 at home) and 1 X86 with these cards. I bought a cheap (DLINK)  
5 port switch for my house and it works fine. The 2 X86s autonegotiate
correctly. My wife's AMD hasn't been turned on since I got the switch a
week ago (any time I upgrade software, she complains that I've changed
everything -- I can't bring myself to tell her that she is one extremely
rare nurse because she feels comfortable running linux). The alpha must be
forced. I boot this machine from SRM only and the boot_osflags string is
"root=/dev/sda3 eth0:fdx autosense=100Mb". This machine uses the tulip
driver.

