very solid distribution.  Everything works:)  (Too bad the symbios
driver I use is in an older version tho ;) treats my ultra2 devices as
ultra, but it doesn't affect performance.  That's a kernel thing, not a
RedHat thing.)

	I went to recompile the stock kernel.  I made very little
changes (the only change I made was to add ext3 support built in and to
change some v4l thingies).  When I try to boot the new kernel, I get
'init not found' and a kernel panic.  It's really quite strange, because
I didn't have this prob with other distros.  Is there a RedHat specific
way of doing things?  Each distro has their own way making it work
better, so I was wondering if this could be attributed to I/O error
(idiot / operator).

Thanks in advance,
Ted





