I have a PC164 upgraded from 2.2.17 to 2.4.9
with the following problem:

Networking works well if X is not used.
When X is started up, networking stops, although 
  ifconfig shows it as being up.
Then, when networking is restarted (service network restart),
X freezes and networking stops...no keyboard, no mouse,
but the display holds that last window view.

I've seen this or a similar problem before in versions
of the kernel prior to 2.2.16 or so.  It went away
with 2.2.16 and 2.2.17, but now appears to be back.

The video card is a S3 trio.  Interrupts for video and
network are different.  The network card is a genuine
Intel Ethernet pro 100+.

Does anyone have any advice about this one?
Is it possible to run a 2.2.17 kernel in 7.2?

Bob Williams




