On Thu, Jun 20, 2002 at 05:35:32PM -0400, Robert Williams wrote:
....
> Is it possible to run a 2.2.17 kernel in 7.2?

If you are not using some file system features (ext3, sparse
superblocks) not supported by 2.2 kernels then running something
from that series should be not a problem.  If you recreated file
system during an installation then you likely have at least
sparse superblocks and block sizes bigger than 1024.  This cannot
be changed without reformatting.

I would pick something later than 2.2.17.  There were security bugs
fixed around 2.2.20.

  Michal




