Hello Michal,

There is a plan, although it is a little fuzzy at this time for HP to create 
and provide updated rpm packages for the the RedHat Linux Alpha 7.2 
distribution.  I hope to have this issue clarified soon.

As a start, I have rebuilt glibc for the ev5, ev56, pca56 and ev67 platforms. 
Glibc for ev6 still has some issues and is being worked upon.  These packages 
are currently available on:

   ftp://alpha.crl.dec.com/pub/linux/redhat/7.2-alpha/hp-updates

Apache with the latest security fix is in the process of being tested.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George

