Hi aaron,

I am running RH 7.2 on a Dell 7150 with two IA64 733 MHz processors.  I use the
machine as a number-cruncher for longrunning FORTRAN programs connected with my
research.   A FORTRAN test program developed on my Alpha 500/333 (actually
EB164 w/333 MHz cpu) runs exactly three times faster on one cpu of the Dell.
Of course, this has something to do with the OS and compiler.  The Alpha runs
DEC Unix 4.0d with a DEC FORTRAN compiler and the Dell has an Intel compiler
for the Itanium.  The Itanium appears to be reliable and error free after three
months of 100%  utilization.

Peter

