Speedracer wrote:

>
> **Warning OT question**
> I notice that some of the RedHat people have been able to get their 
> hands on the ia64 for development.  Since some of those people 
> frequest this list I'm curious as to their opinions of the chip and 
> how does it compare to the alphas?  I'm curious to get some first hand 
> reports back on machines running RH, and the capabilites of the ia64.
> Has anyone else had experience with the ia64 besides the RH people? 
> (I'd really LOVE to hear from someone that has seen IA64 do any VMS 
> stuff) 

Before I start, I need to point out that the Alpha has been a production 
chip for quite a number of years. The ia64's that I'm using are 
preproduction and consequently will likely not have been well optimized.

In terms of everyday use, I'd say that the 667Mhz 21264 on my desk is 
slightly faster than the 950 Mhz ia64 I'm also using. I can't explain 
why there would be this much disparity, simply that it exists. I've run 
no benchmarks on either box though as that would just be somewhat 
meaningless at this stage of the ia64 development cycle. Certainly the 
devlopment tools (gcc, binutils etc) are still being improved.

I'd adopt a wait and see approach to that question as it's really too 
early to tell.

Phil
