Finally got back to looking into this.  First off, let me apologize if
some of my previous messages sounded a bit harsh.  The problem I was
having with the previous suggestions was that they were simply an
incantation with no explanation of why it should fix the problem or what
to do if it didn't fix the problem.  When they didn't work, I had no
idea where else to go.  The following message was a bit different
because it gave me some idea of the works behind the steps I had been
given.

It turned out to be a low tech problem after all.  It appears that the
disc one I downloaded was no good.  The install got an MD5sum mismatch
error attempting to unpack the kernel RPM so there were no files in
/lib/modules/2.4.9-32/kernel/drivers/scsi.  I downloaded the disc again
and everything installed with no problem and I can now boot off the
disk.  So on to the next problem ... X will not run because it no longer
supports the Number 9 GXE S3 card.  I need to find a different ISA card
to use or go back to the older version of XFree86 until I can replace
the card.  At least the command line now works.  Anyone have
instructions on how to go back to the older version of X?  The ones I've
found so far do not seem to work - but I've not searched much yet.

