Hi!

Nelson Brito wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> -> Could some one recommend a method or software to do it?
> 
> I don't know if you can write to a dvd with dd but it must
> be possible since "on Unix every device is a file :-)".
> I'd use it.

AFAIK, a 'write()' to a CD writer will fail, they have to be 
instructed via some 'ioctl()' - the sources of "cdrecord" 
would show that.

However, at home I use "cdrecord" to copy a block device 
(a partition with a FAT file system) onto CD. 
So IMHO a combination of 
   dd if=/dev/the_DAT_drive ibs=... | cdrecord ... 
might do the trick, and if "cdrecord" wants a file name there 
is still the chance to use a named pipe ("FIFO").

HTH, 
Joerg Bruehe

