Hi,

I don't know much about debugging with gdb.  But, I did compare g77 to
Intel's Fortran compiler 5.0 for Linux on an IA64 platform running
RH7.2.  The code I tested is mature and has run for years on six
different systems.  The runtime difference was astounding.  The code
compiled with the Intel compiler ran exactly twice as fast as that
compiled by the g77 that came in RH7.2 for the Itanium.  I compiled
using the best available optimization options in both compilers.

Peter

