> cpus detected           : 0
> 
> What I can't figure out is what kind of 'arch' this is: alpha, alphaev5,
> alphaev56, ... ? Can someone help me out?
> 
> What are those 'ev*', anyway?

EV5 was the second generation Alpha, EV56 was the first shrink of EV5 and 
also included new byte word instructions, PCA56 was an EV56 with 
additional instructions (aimed at multimedia work) but had smaller cache 
sizes. 

So, you have an alphapca56. Hope that helps,
