Danilo Godec <danci@kibla.org> writes:

> I have an 164SX machine with 533 MHz processor. Here is the /proc/cpuinfo:
> 
> [danci@alfonz danci]$ cat /proc/cpuinfo
> cpu                     : Alpha
> cpu model               : PCA56
>
> What I can't figure out is what kind of 'arch' this is: alpha, alphaev5,
> alphaev56, ... ? Can someone help me out?

It's a pca56, aka 21164pc. The pca56 is based on the ev56 and adds
some multimedia instructions, but lacks on-chip scache (for cost
reasons). The model naming is like this:

Core    AKA
EV4     21064
EV45    21064A

EV5     21164
EV56    21164A
PCA56   21164PC

EV6     21264
EV67    21264A
EV68    21264B

EV7     21364

-- 
	Falk




