Hi,

I no longer have use for a perfectly good alpha box, as I just replaced
it with a Dell 7150 with 8GB of RAM.  I have no idea what the alpha is
worth at this point.  The specifications are:

EB164 - 333MHz
2MB Cache
SRM Console V4.8-1
DECchip 21164-5
DECchip 21171 CIA ASIC Pass 2
DECchip 21040 Network Controller
NCR 53C875 SCSI Controller (or Symbios Logic C810 SCSI host adapter) -
not sure which
Seagate ST32550W (2GB)
Seagate ST15150W (4GB)
Toshiba SCSI CDROM
HP C1533A DAT2
S3 TRIO graphics
Intel 82378IB PCI-to-ISA bridge
256MB DEC/COMPAQ installed RAM
400W Antron power supply
10 opening metal tower
NT 4.0 SP4 installed on the 2GB drive
UNIX 4.0d on the 4GB drive.
License for OSF/1
License for DEC FORTRAN 90

I plan to remove the DAT2 drive to use as a backup for my new system, if
it turns out to be compatible with the Dell SCSI.  Unless someone has a
standalone DAT to trade.

I guess I won't get much.  But, I thought I would give it a try.

Peter





