Greetings,

During the short time frame between the release of the original ISO images
and the creation of the media kits, which will be available for purchase
from HP, a few important problems were discovered.
 
1) Floppy DMA problems on large memory systems (>2GB).
2) Errata due to issues encountered by RedHat.
 
A new set of ISO images have been created for the media kits that fixes
these problems. These new images are identifed with a "20020627" tag that
indicates that all the updates, which are available on the ftp sites through
the end of the day on June 27, 2002 are included in theses ISO images.
 
If you have downloaded a previos set of ISO images, you will only need to
download and install the updated rpms from
 
ftp://alpha.crl.dec.com/pub/linux/redhat/7.2-alpha/updates
      

Best Regards,


--George




